# 🎯 Advantages of Excel

- Beginner-friendly
- No programming required
- Excellent for business reporting
- Large library of built-in functions
- Powerful visualization tools
- Easy to share and collaborate
- Supported by almost every organization

---

# ⚠️ Limitations of Excel

While Excel is powerful, it also has limitations.

- Not suitable for very large datasets
- Manual processes can lead to errors
- Limited automation compared to Python
- Version control can be difficult
- Complex workbooks may become slow

As datasets grow, analysts often combine Excel with SQL, Python, and Power BI.

---

# 💡 Best Practices

- Keep raw data separate from reports.
- Use Excel Tables instead of plain ranges.
- Avoid hardcoding values in formulas.
- Name worksheets clearly.
- Document important calculations.
- Save versions of critical workbooks.
- Validate data before analysis.

